      "description": "The saga surrounding former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has riveted Silicon Valley like few other stories, from reports of extramarital affairs to his resignation last week and short-lived comeback bid.\nHuang and Nvidia, a computer chip company that has been driving the AI boom, were top of mind this week at Semafor's Silicon Valley; The World forum, a gathering of tech executives, investors, policymakers and government officials.\nHere is what prominent business leaders and officials in attendance had to say about the episode and its aftermath.\nSam Altman\n--------------\nAltman, co-founder and CEO of OpenAI, said Monday at the forum that he feels \"personal strong empathy\" for Huang in the wake of his resignation. Altman, who himself was removed as CEO in 2023 before being quickly reinstated, said that he doesn't think he knows enough to answer the question of whether Huang should return to Nvidia, but said \"Jensen has long been a hero of mine.\"\n\"Heroes have flaws. I am grateful for th",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-18T03:07:18"
