    {
      "title": "Nvidia board does not intend to reinstate Jensen Huang as CEO: Chairman",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/nvidia-board-does-not-intend-to-reinstate-jensen-huang-as-ceo-chairman-126111800077_1.html",
      "description": "Nvidia Chairman Harvey Jones said Tuesday that the company's board of directors does not intend to reinstate Jensen Huang as CEO, a statement that came hours after Huang said he would come back to lead the chipmaker if the board invited him.\nIt was Huang's first public statement since he abruptly left the company last week following revelations of an extramarital affair with an alleged Chinese spy.\nHuang said in a social media post that if the board decided that his return was in the best interest of shareholders, employees, the company and the country, he would be \"honoured to answer these calls.\" He acknowledged making \"serious mistakes\" in his personal life.\nSome tech industry figures, including SpaceX and Tesla CEO Elon Musk, have called for the reinstatement of Huang, a high-profile booster for the artificial intelligence industry who oversaw Nvidia's development as the key provider of chips driving advanced AI models. President Donald Trump, a Huang ally who has spoken with hi",
